      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe intended order might be one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
